,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);padding:20px 16px 48px;line-height:1.6}.tr{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;margin:0}.cr{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.ar{direction:rtl;text-align:right}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main class=\"sp\"><nav class=\"crumbs\"><a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> › <a href=\"/en/surah/56.html\">Surah Al-Waaqia</a> › Verse 29</nav><h1>Tafsir of Surah Al-Waaqia 56:29</h1><p class=\"vt ar\" lang=\"ar\">﴿وَطَلْحٍ مَّنضُودٍ﴾</p><section><h3>Translation of the meaning</h3><p class=\"tr\">And [banana] trees layered [with fruit]</p><span class=\"cr\" dir=\"ltr\">English Translation - Noor International Center — v1.1.2 · QuranEnc.com</span></section><p class=\"cr\">The words of the two imams are given in their original Arabic, verbatim, with references.</p><section><h2>Imam Ibn al-Qayyim</h2><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\">والمنضود: هو الذي قد نضد بعضه على بعض، كالمشط.<cite>«زاد المعاد في هدي خير العباد» 4/309</cite></blockquote><h3>What he quoted from others</h3><blockquote class=\"ar\" lang=\"ar\"><span class=\"who\">أكثر المفسرين</span> <span class=\"st\">حكاه</span> «قال أكثر المفسرين، هو الموز. والمنضود: هو الذي قد نضد بعضه على بعض»<cite>«زاد المعاد في هدي خير العباد» 4/309</cite></blockquote></section><a class=\"btn pri open\" href=\"/tafsir.html?lang=en#s56a29\">Open in the interactive tafsir (full texts)</a><div class=\"pn\"><a href=\"/en/ayah/56-26.html\">Previous verse (56:26)</a><a href=\"/en/ayah/56-35.html\">Next verse (56:35)</a></div></main><footer class=\"site-foot\"><span>Tafsir al-Shaykhayn · <a href=\"/en/\">Home</a> · <a href=\"/about.html\">About the project</a> · <a href=\"/privacy.html\">Privacy &amp; terms</a></span><a href=\"https://doersadv.com\" rel=\"noopener\" dir=\"ltr\">Developed by Doers</a></footer>\n</body>\n</html>\n","ayah/56-35.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Tafsir of Al-Waaqia 56: